IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `maireg-dates`

-- Motor Accident Injuries Regulation 2017 (NSW) -- the costs provisions (Part 6, Schedules 1, 2 and 3), from the seat of
-- the claimant.
--
-- SEAT: the claimant. Every exported question is one that person would ask: "What is a monetary unit worth?", "What is
-- the most my lawyer may charge for this step, or for my damages claim?", "What if I signed a costs agreement?", "What if
-- I claimed as a child?", "What is the most a doctor may charge for a report?", "Can I claim my treating doctor's first
-- report?", "Is this cost outside the caps?", "Who pays the costs if I rejected the assessment and went to court?",
-- "Must the insurer pay my costs?", "What must the insurer pay for my treatment?", "What can GST add?". Lawyers, doctors,
-- the insurer, the Authority and the Commission get no seat here.
--
-- Provisions: cl 20 (costs outside the Part), cl 21-26 (maximum legal costs, internal review, compensation matter
-- applications, exempt claims, costs agreements, minors), cl 27-28 (medico-legal fees), cl 30-31 (costs after a claims
-- assessment), cl 34 (treatment fees), cl 35 (GST); Schedule 1 Parts 1 and 2 (except the country and interstate
-- loadings), Schedule 2, Schedule 3 cl 1-3. Out: see NOTES.md.
--
-- MONEY. Amounts are in Australian dollars. Schedule 3 sets the monetary unit by adjustment year (from 1 October); its
-- formula was lost from the deposited text, so the encoding uses the "Editorial note" table of amounts that the
-- deposited text does carry (2017-18 to 2024-25). A date outside those years answers NOTHING.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 22 September 2023; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Accident Injuries Regulation 2017 -- costs`

§§ `The nouns`

-- Schedule 1 Part 1: the dispute-resolution and court steps a lawyer may act in, and the internal review of cl 23.
DECLARE `The step my lawyer acted in` IS ONE OF
    `an internal review by the insurer`
    `a merit review of a regulated merit review matter`
    `a review panel review of a merit review decision`
    `a medical assessment`
    `a further medical assessment under s 7.24`
    `a review panel review of a medical assessment under s 7.26`
    `a miscellaneous claims assessment of a regulated matter`
    `representation at an assessment conference under s 7.46`
    `a conference directly related to a claims assessment or court hearing`
    `interlocutory court proceedings`
    `representation in court by an advocate other than senior counsel`
    `representation in court by senior counsel`
    `court proceedings on a compensation matter application`
    `representation on a compensation matter application by an advocate other than senior counsel`
    `representation on a compensation matter application by senior counsel`
    `a conference directly related to a compensation matter application`

-- Schedule 1 Part 2: how the claim for damages ended.
DECLARE `How my damages claim ended` IS ONE OF
    `resolved without a certificate of claims assessment`
    `resolved after a certificate of claims assessment, without court proceedings`
    `finalised after court proceedings began`

-- The two kinds of claim.
DECLARE `The kind of my claim` IS ONE OF
    `statutory benefits`
    `damages`

-- Schedule 2: the medico-legal services.
DECLARE `The medico-legal service` IS ONE OF
    `giving evidence other than expert evidence`
    `giving expert evidence`
    `travel by private car to give evidence`
    `accommodation and meals to give evidence`
    `a report by a treating general practitioner, without re-examining me`
    `a report by a treating general practitioner, re-examining me`
    `a report by a treating specialist, without re-examining me`
    `a report by a treating specialist, re-examining me`
    `a report by a specialist who has not treated me, not jointly appointed, without examining me`
    `a report by a specialist who has not treated me, not jointly appointed, examining me`
    `a report by a specialist who has not treated me, jointly appointed, without examining me`
    `a report by a specialist who has not treated me, jointly appointed, examining me`
    `copying medical reports`

-- cl 20: the costs the Part does not regulate.
DECLARE `The cost I am asking about` IS ONE OF
    `an accident investigator's or accident reconstruction report`
    `an accountant's report`
    `a report from a health practitioner who is not a medical practitioner`
    `another professional report about treatment or rehabilitation`
    `clinical records of a treating health practitioner`
    `interpreter or translation services`
    `a police report`
    `a fee or charge under the Government Information (Public Access) Act 2009`
    `court fees`
    `my travel to attend the Commission or a court`
    `witness expenses at the Commission or a court`
    `another cost`

-- cl 30: who pays the costs after court.
DECLARE `Who pays the costs after court` IS ONE OF
    `clause 30 does not apply, because I accepted the assessed damages within 21 days`
    `the court's direction as to costs decides`
    `I must pay the costs any party incurred, up to the cap`
    `the insurer must pay the costs any party incurred`
    `the insurer and I each pay our own costs`

§§ `Schedule 3 -- the monetary unit`

-- Sch 3 cl 1 "adjustment year means a period of 12 months commencing on 1 October." cl 2(1)(a) "in the adjustment year
-- 2017-18--$100"; (b) later years by a CPI formula that the deposited text lost; the deposited "Editorial note" gives the
-- amounts to 2024-25. cl 2(3): never less than the year before (the table already respects it).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the adjustment year beginning in` `the day` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day` AT LEAST 10 THEN DATE_YEAR `the day` ELSE DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS 1

@export What is a monetary unit worth on a given day, for the Regulation's maximum costs and fees (Schedule 3)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the cost or fee is charged or the service provided
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is a monetary unit worth on this day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the year` EQUALS 2017 THEN JUST 100
           IF `the year` EQUALS 2018 THEN JUST 102.06
           IF `the year` EQUALS 2019 THEN JUST 103.76
           IF `the year` EQUALS 2020 THEN JUST 103.76
           IF `the year` EQUALS 2021 THEN JUST 106.89
           IF `the year` EQUALS 2022 THEN JUST 112.53
           IF `the year` EQUALS 2023 THEN JUST 119.96
           IF `the year` EQUALS 2024 THEN JUST 124.53
           OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (before 1 October 2017 the Schedule names no amount; after 30 September 2025 the amount is not in the deposited text)
    WHERE
        `the year` MEANS `the adjustment year beginning in` `the day`

-- Sch 3 cl 3: a maximum calculated by reference to a monetary unit "is to be rounded to the nearest dollar (and an amount
-- of 50 cents is to be rounded down)". The whole of a maximum is rounded once (fork F11).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `the monetary units` IS A NUMBER, `the dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the rounded maximum on` `the day` `of` `the monetary units` `plus` `the dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What is a monetary unit worth on this day` `the day`
    WHEN JUST `the unit` THEN JUST (`rounded to the nearest dollar, 50 cents down` ((`the monetary units` TIMES `the unit`) PLUS `the dollars`))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `cl 20 -- costs outside the Part`

-- cl 20 "Costs referred to in this Part (Division 4 excepted) do not include any of the following" (a)-(k).
@export Is this cost left outside the Regulation's maximum legal costs and fees, so that the caps do not reach it (cl 20)?
GIVEN `the cost` IS A `The cost I am asking about` @desc The cost you are asking about. One of: "an accident investigator's or accident reconstruction report", "an accountant's report", "a report from a health practitioner who is not a medical practitioner", "another professional report about treatment or rehabilitation" (for example an architect's report on home modifications), "clinical records of a treating health practitioner", "interpreter or translation services", "a police report", "a fee or charge under the Government Information (Public Access) Act 2009", "court fees", "my travel to attend the Commission or a court", "witness expenses at the Commission or a court", "another cost"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is this cost outside the caps` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the cost`
    WHEN `another cost` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: the cost may or may not be one the Part regulates)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Schedule 1 Part 1, cl 22-24 -- maximum costs for dispute resolution and court steps`

-- cl 22(1): Schedule 1 sets "the maximum costs recoverable by Australian legal practitioners and claimants", on any basis
-- (cl 21). cl 23: "no costs are payable for legal services provided to a claimant ... in connection with an application
-- for internal review". cl 23A: no costs for legal services on a compensation matter application concerning a claim for
-- damages, "to the extent that the costs are payable on a practitioner and client basis". cl 24(1): the Schedule 1
-- maxima "do not apply" to a claim exempt from assessment under s 7.34 (NOTHING: no cap is fixed).
-- Schedule 1 cl 1(1), 2(1), 3(1): 16 monetary units "(to a maximum of 60 monetary units per claim)"; cl 1(3), 2(2), 2(3):
-- 16 units if the President approves the referral, otherwise nil to the applicant and 8 to the respondent; cl 4: 30 units
-- flat at an assessment conference plus 3 an hour beyond 2 hours, and 3 an hour for a conference; cl 5: 8 units for
-- interlocutory proceedings, 25 or 35.5 a day in court; cl 6: 10 units for compensation matter application proceedings,
-- 25 or 35.5 a day, 3 for a conference (no "per hour": fork F12). cl 5 and 6(2): senior counsel's fees "not to be
-- included unless the court so orders".
@export What is the most my lawyer may charge or recover for this dispute-resolution or court step in my motor accident claim (cl 22-24; Schedule 1 Part 1)?
GIVEN `the step` IS A `The step my lawyer acted in` @desc The step. One of: "an internal review by the insurer", "a merit review of a regulated merit review matter", "a review panel review of a merit review decision", "a medical assessment", "a further medical assessment under s 7.24", "a review panel review of a medical assessment under s 7.26", "a miscellaneous claims assessment of a regulated matter", "representation at an assessment conference under s 7.46", "a conference directly related to a claims assessment or court hearing", "interlocutory court proceedings", "representation in court by an advocate other than senior counsel", "representation in court by senior counsel", "court proceedings on a compensation matter application", "representation on a compensation matter application by an advocate other than senior counsel", "representation on a compensation matter application by senior counsel", "a conference directly related to a compensation matter application"
      `how many` IS A NUMBER @desc How many: for merit reviews, medical assessments and miscellaneous claims assessments, how many of that kind on this claim so far, including this one; for an assessment conference or a conference, the hours; for representation in court, the days; otherwise 1
      `the President approved the referral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a review panel review or a further medical assessment: whether the President approved the application for referral
      `I applied for the referral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a review panel review or a further medical assessment: whether you (rather than the insurer) applied for the referral
      `the court ordered senior counsel fees to be included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For senior counsel: whether the court ordered that fees for senior counsel (or more than one advocate) be included
      `my claim is exempt from claims assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is exempt from claims assessment under section 7.34 of the Act (for example because you are under legal incapacity)
      `my claim is for` IS A `The kind of my claim` @desc Whether the claim is for "statutory benefits" or for "damages"
      `the costs are charged to me under my own lawyer's retainer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs are ones you pay your own lawyer (practitioner and client), rather than costs recovered from the other side (party and party)
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the legal service was provided (fixes the value of a monetary unit)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most my lawyer may charge for this step` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `my claim is exempt from claims assessment` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (cl 24(1): the maxima do not apply; no cap is fixed)
           IF `the step` EQUALS `an internal review by the insurer` THEN JUST 0  -- cl 23
           IF `compensation matter step` AND `my claim is for` EQUALS `damages` AND `the costs are charged to me under my own lawyer's retainer`
           THEN JUST 0  -- cl 23A
           OTHERWISE `the rounded maximum on` `the day` `of` `the step units` `plus` 0
    WHERE
        `compensation matter step` MEANS
               `the step` EQUALS `court proceedings on a compensation matter application`
            OR `the step` EQUALS `representation on a compensation matter application by an advocate other than senior counsel`
            OR `the step` EQUALS `representation on a compensation matter application by senior counsel`
            OR `the step` EQUALS `a conference directly related to a compensation matter application`
        `on referral` MEANS
            IF `the President approved the referral` THEN 16
            ELSE IF `I applied for the referral` THEN 0 ELSE 8
        `senior counsel` MEANS
            IF `the court ordered senior counsel fees to be included` THEN 35.5 TIMES `how many` ELSE 0
        `the step units` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the step`
            WHEN `a merit review of a regulated merit review matter` THEN `the smaller of` (16 TIMES `how many`) `and` 60
            WHEN `a review panel review of a merit review decision` THEN `on referral`
            WHEN `a medical assessment` THEN `the smaller of` (16 TIMES `how many`) `and` 60
            WHEN `a further medical assessment under s 7.24` THEN `on referral`
            WHEN `a review panel review of a medical assessment under s 7.26` THEN `on referral`
            WHEN `a miscellaneous claims assessment of a regulated matter` THEN `the smaller of` (16 TIMES `how many`) `and` 60
            WHEN `representation at an assessment conference under s 7.46` THEN 30 PLUS (3 TIMES (`the larger of` 0 `and` (`how many` MINUS 2)))
            WHEN `a conference directly related to a claims assessment or court hearing` THEN 3 TIMES `how many`
            WHEN `interlocutory court proceedings` THEN 8
            WHEN `representation in court by an advocate other than senior counsel` THEN 25 TIMES `how many`
            WHEN `representation in court by senior counsel` THEN `senior counsel`
            WHEN `court proceedings on a compensation matter application` THEN 10
            WHEN `representation on a compensation matter application by an advocate other than senior counsel` THEN 25 TIMES `how many`
            WHEN `representation on a compensation matter application by senior counsel` THEN `senior counsel`
            WHEN `a conference directly related to a compensation matter application` THEN 3
            OTHERWISE 0

§§ `Schedule 1 Part 2 -- maximum costs for the stages of a claim for damages`

-- Table A, stage 3 (for a lawyer acting for the claimant), as a function of the resolution amount R and whether the
-- insurer wholly admitted liability: (a) R <= $20,000, admitted: 7.24 units; (b) R <= $20,000, not admitted: 10 cents a
-- dollar; (c) $20,000 < R <= $50,000, admitted: 7.24 units + 12 cents a dollar over $20,000; (d) the same, not admitted:
-- 25.92 units + 12 cents; (e) $50,000 < R <= $100,000, admitted: 51.84 units + 10 cents a dollar over $50,000; (f) not
-- admitted: 71.28 units + 10 cents; (g) R > $100,000, admitted: 114.48 units + 2 cents a dollar over $100,000; (h) not
-- admitted: 133.92 units + 2 cents. Returned as (monetary units, dollars).
DECLARE `Units and dollars` HAS
    `units` IS A NUMBER
    `dollars` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN r IS A NUMBER, `admitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Units and dollars`
`stage 3 of Table A on` r `admitted` MEANS
    BRANCH IF r AT MOST 20000 AND `admitted` THEN `Units and dollars` WITH `units` IS 7.24, `dollars` IS 0
           IF r AT MOST 20000 THEN `Units and dollars` WITH `units` IS 0, `dollars` IS r TIMES 0.10
           IF r AT MOST 50000 AND `admitted` THEN `Units and dollars` WITH `units` IS 7.24, `dollars` IS (r MINUS 20000) TIMES 0.12
           IF r AT MOST 50000 THEN `Units and dollars` WITH `units` IS 25.92, `dollars` IS (r MINUS 20000) TIMES 0.12
           IF r AT MOST 100000 AND `admitted` THEN `Units and dollars` WITH `units` IS 51.84, `dollars` IS (r MINUS 50000) TIMES 0.10
           IF r AT MOST 100000 THEN `Units and dollars` WITH `units` IS 71.28, `dollars` IS (r MINUS 50000) TIMES 0.10
           IF `admitted` THEN `Units and dollars` WITH `units` IS 114.48, `dollars` IS (r MINUS 100000) TIMES 0.02
           OTHERWISE `Units and dollars` WITH `units` IS 133.92, `dollars` IS (r MINUS 100000) TIMES 0.02

-- Table B, stage 2, on the settlement or award amount S: S <= $20,000: nil; $20,000 < S <= $50,000: 10 cents a dollar
-- over $20,000; $50,000 < S <= $100,000: 37.8 units + 8 cents a dollar over $50,000; S > $100,000: 88.56 units + 2 cents
-- a dollar over $100,000.
GIVEN s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Units and dollars`
`stage 2 of Table B on` s MEANS
    BRANCH IF s AT MOST 20000 THEN `Units and dollars` WITH `units` IS 0, `dollars` IS 0
           IF s AT MOST 50000 THEN `Units and dollars` WITH `units` IS 0, `dollars` IS (s MINUS 20000) TIMES 0.10
           IF s AT MOST 100000 THEN `Units and dollars` WITH `units` IS 37.8, `dollars` IS (s MINUS 50000) TIMES 0.08
           OTHERWISE `Units and dollars` WITH `units` IS 88.56, `dollars` IS (s MINUS 100000) TIMES 0.02

-- Sch 1 Part 2 cl 2(1)-(5). Table A for a lawyer acting for the claimant: stage 1 (to service of the notice of claim)
-- 2.92 units; stage 2 (to the response to the insurer's s 6.22 offer) 4.32 units; then stage 3 if resolved without a
-- certificate, or stage 4 (stage 3 worked on the assessment amount "as if that assessment were the resolution amount",
-- plus 2 cents a dollar of the assessment amount) if resolved after a certificate without court, or stage 5 (stage 4 plus
-- 2 cents a dollar of the settlement or award amount) if finalised after court proceedings began. cl 2(3) "Costs may be
-- charged for more than one stage": stages 1 and 2 are added (fork F13). cl 2(2), Table B, where the lawyer was first
-- retained after the certificate: stage 1 (advice on the certificate) 3.56 units plus stage 2. cl 2(5): "an award of
-- damages" is the award "after deducting the amount of any statutory benefits paid under Division 3.3" (weekly
-- payments). cl 24(1): no maxima for an exempt claim (NOTHING). Not for claims for statutory benefits (Part 2 is "for
-- claims for damages").
@export What is the most my lawyer may charge or recover for my claim for damages, adding up the stages Schedule 1 Part 2 allows (cl 22, 24; Schedule 1 Part 2)?
GIVEN `my claim is exempt from claims assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is exempt from claims assessment under section 7.34 of the Act
      `my lawyer was first retained after the certificate of claims assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you first retained your lawyer only after the certificate of claims assessment was issued under section 7.36
      `how my claim ended` IS A `How my damages claim ended` @desc How the claim ended. One of: "resolved without a certificate of claims assessment", "resolved after a certificate of claims assessment, without court proceedings", "finalised after court proceedings began"
      `the insurer wholly admitted liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer wholly admitted liability for your claim
      `the amount my claim was resolved for` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount paid in resolution of the claim (the settlement, or the court's award of damages), in dollars
      `it was resolved by a court award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim ended with a court's award of damages rather than a settlement
      `the weekly statutory benefits paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly payments of statutory benefits (Division 3.3 of the Act) paid to you, in dollars (used only where the claim ended with an award)
      `the amount of the claims assessment` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of damages in the certificate of claims assessment, in dollars (0 if there was none)
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the costs are charged (fixes the value of a monetary unit)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most my lawyer may charge for my damages claim` MEANS
    IF `my claim is exempt from claims assessment`
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (cl 24(1): the maxima do not apply; no cap is fixed)
    ELSE IF `my lawyer was first retained after the certificate of claims assessment`
         THEN `the rounded maximum on` `the day` `of` (3.56 PLUS `table B`'s units) `plus` (`table B`'s dollars)
         ELSE CONSIDER `how my claim ended`
              WHEN `resolved without a certificate of claims assessment`
              THEN `the rounded maximum on` `the day` `of` (7.24 PLUS `stage 3`'s units) `plus` (`stage 3`'s dollars)
              WHEN `resolved after a certificate of claims assessment, without court proceedings`
              THEN `the rounded maximum on` `the day` `of` (7.24 PLUS `on the assessment`'s units) `plus` (`the stage 4 dollars`)
              WHEN `finalised after court proceedings began`
              THEN `the rounded maximum on` `the day` `of` (7.24 PLUS `on the assessment`'s units) `plus` (`the stage 4 dollars` PLUS (`the settlement or award` TIMES 0.02))
    WHERE
        `the settlement or award` MEANS
            IF `it was resolved by a court award`
            THEN `the amount my claim was resolved for` MINUS `the weekly statutory benefits paid to me`
            ELSE `the amount my claim was resolved for`
        `table B` MEANS `stage 2 of Table B on` `the settlement or award`
        `stage 3` MEANS `stage 3 of Table A on` `the settlement or award` `the insurer wholly admitted liability`
        `on the assessment` MEANS `stage 3 of Table A on` `the amount of the claims assessment` `the insurer wholly admitted liability`
        `the stage 4 dollars` MEANS (`on the assessment`'s dollars) PLUS (`the amount of the claims assessment` TIMES 0.02)

§§ `cl 25 -- costs agreements`

-- cl 25(1): Schedule 1 does not apply to practitioner and client costs if (a) the lawyer made the Uniform Law disclosure,
-- (b) entered a costs agreement (not a conditional costs agreement with an uplift premium), (c) first advised in a
-- separate written document that the party pays any excess over the Act's amount, (d) for a claimant, gives the Authority
-- a costs breakdown when the claim is finalised, and (e) "the amount paid in resolution of the claim by way of settlement
-- or an award of damages is more than $75,000". (2) "However, the maximum costs recoverable ... on a practitioner and
-- client basis are fixed at the amount calculated by subtracting $75,000 from the amount paid in resolution of the
-- claim." (3) That amount includes party and party costs. (5) Not for a claim for statutory benefits.
@export If I signed a costs agreement with my lawyer, what is the most my lawyer may charge me for my claim for damages (cl 25)?
GIVEN `my claim is for` IS A `The kind of my claim` @desc Whether the claim is for "statutory benefits" or for "damages"
      `my lawyer made the costs disclosure the Uniform Law requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your lawyer gave you the costs disclosure required by Division 3 of Part 4.3 of the Legal Profession Uniform Law
      `I signed a costs agreement that is not a conditional agreement with an uplift` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you entered into a costs agreement with your lawyer under Division 4 of Part 4.3 of the Uniform Law, other than a conditional ("no win, no fee") agreement providing for an uplift premium on success
      `my lawyer first told me in a separate document that I pay any excess` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before you signed, your lawyer told you in a separate written document that even if costs are awarded to you, you will have to pay any amount of the agreed costs above what the Act would allow
      `my lawyer gave the Authority a costs breakdown when the claim was finalised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your lawyer gave the State Insurance Regulatory Authority a costs breakdown for the claim when it was finalised
      `the amount paid in resolution of my claim` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount paid to resolve your claim by settlement or award of damages, including any party and party costs paid with it, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most my lawyer may charge under a costs agreement` MEANS
    IF     `my claim is for` EQUALS `damages`
       AND `my lawyer made the costs disclosure the Uniform Law requires`
       AND `I signed a costs agreement that is not a conditional agreement with an uplift`
       AND `my lawyer first told me in a separate document that I pay any excess`
       AND `my lawyer gave the Authority a costs breakdown when the claim was finalised`
       AND `the amount paid in resolution of my claim` GREATER THAN 75000
    THEN JUST (`the amount paid in resolution of my claim` MINUS 75000)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (cl 25 does not lift the Schedule 1 maxima; they apply instead)

§§ `cl 26 -- claims by minors`

-- cl 26(1): for an "exempt minor claim", the maximum costs "(unless otherwise ordered by the court)" are (a) $5,000;
-- (b) $10,000 if the resolution amount is more than $25,000 but not more than $50,000 and no associate has claimed;
-- (c) $15,000 if more than $50,000 but not more than $75,000 and no associate has claimed. (2) An exempt minor claim is
-- one certified exempt "solely on the ground that the claimant is ... under the age of 18 years". (3) An associate was an
-- occupant of the same vehicle and retained the same law practice. (4) Not where the amount is more than $75,000. These
-- dollar amounts are not indexed.
@export If my claim was exempt from claims assessment only because I was under 18, what is the most my lawyer may charge for it (cl 26)?
GIVEN `my claim was certified exempt only because I was under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a certificate under section 7.34 of the Act made your claim exempt from claims assessment solely because you were under 18 on the day it was issued
      `the amount paid in resolution of my claim` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount paid to finally resolve your claim (settlement, award or otherwise), in dollars
      `an associate of mine has claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone who was in the same vehicle as you at the time of the accident has made a claim for the accident and retained the same law practice as you
      `the court ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court made an order setting the costs differently
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most my lawyer may charge for my claim as a minor` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `my claim was certified exempt only because I was under 18`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside cl 26's scope)
           IF `the amount paid in resolution of my claim` GREATER THAN 75000 THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (cl 26(4): the clause does not apply; it sets no cap)
           IF `the court ordered otherwise` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the court's order decides)
           IF `an associate of mine has claimed` THEN JUST 5000
           IF `the amount paid in resolution of my claim` GREATER THAN 50000 THEN JUST 15000
           IF `the amount paid in resolution of my claim` GREATER THAN 25000 THEN JUST 10000
           OTHERWISE JUST 5000

§§ `cl 27, 28, Schedule 2 -- medico-legal fees`

-- Schedule 2: 1 non-expert evidence 4.5 units an hour "(or proportionately if not for a full hour) to a maximum of 9";
-- 2 expert evidence 12 units for the first 1.5 hours (travel included) and 4.5 an hour after (proportionately), "to a
-- maximum of 36"; 3 travel 66 cents a kilometre; 4 accommodation and meals "reasonable costs" (a judgment: NOTHING);
-- 5-8 reports (3.75, 4.95, 12, 16, 12, 16, 18, 22 units); 9 copying $1 a page; 10 a cancelled appearance or report "Not
-- more than 50% of the relevant amount". Expert evidence shorter than 1.5 hours still gets the 12 units (fork F14).
@export What is the most a health practitioner may charge for this medical report or appearance as a witness in my motor accident matter (cl 27, 28(1); Schedule 2)?
GIVEN `the service` IS A `The medico-legal service` @desc The service. One of: "giving evidence other than expert evidence", "giving expert evidence", "travel by private car to give evidence", "accommodation and meals to give evidence", "a report by a treating general practitioner, without re-examining me", "a report by a treating general practitioner, re-examining me", "a report by a treating specialist, without re-examining me", "a report by a treating specialist, re-examining me", "a report by a specialist who has not treated me, not jointly appointed, without examining me", "a report by a specialist who has not treated me, not jointly appointed, examining me", "a report by a specialist who has not treated me, jointly appointed, without examining me", "a report by a specialist who has not treated me, jointly appointed, examining me", "copying medical reports"
      `how many` IS A NUMBER @desc For evidence, the hours (for expert evidence including travel to and from court); for travel, the kilometres; for copying, the pages; otherwise 1
      `it was cancelled as not required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the appearance or report was cancelled because it was not required
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day of the service (fixes the value of a monetary unit)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most a health practitioner may charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the full fee`
    WHEN JUST `fee` THEN IF `it was cancelled as not required` THEN JUST (`fee` TIMES 50%) ELSE JUST `fee`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        `in units` u MEANS `the rounded maximum on` `the day` `of` u `plus` 0
        `the full fee` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the service`
            WHEN `giving evidence other than expert evidence` THEN `in units` (`the smaller of` (4.5 TIMES `how many`) `and` 9)
            WHEN `giving expert evidence` THEN `in units` (`the smaller of` (12 PLUS (4.5 TIMES (`the larger of` 0 `and` (`how many` MINUS 1.5)))) `and` 36)
            WHEN `travel by private car to give evidence` THEN JUST (`how many` TIMES 0.66)
            WHEN `accommodation and meals to give evidence` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind ("reasonable costs": a judgment)
            WHEN `a report by a treating general practitioner, without re-examining me` THEN `in units` 3.75
            WHEN `a report by a treating general practitioner, re-examining me` THEN `in units` 4.95
            WHEN `a report by a treating specialist, without re-examining me` THEN `in units` 12
            WHEN `a report by a treating specialist, re-examining me` THEN `in units` 16
            WHEN `a report by a specialist who has not treated me, not jointly appointed, without examining me` THEN `in units` 12
            WHEN `a report by a specialist who has not treated me, not jointly appointed, examining me` THEN `in units` 16
            WHEN `a report by a specialist who has not treated me, jointly appointed, without examining me` THEN `in units` 18
            WHEN `a report by a specialist who has not treated me, jointly appointed, examining me` THEN `in units` 22
            WHEN `copying medical reports` THEN JUST `how many`
            OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- cl 28(3) "A claimant may not claim an amount set out in item 5 or 6 (relating to reports by treating medical
-- practitioners) of Schedule 2 in respect of an initial report by a treating medical practitioner unless the claimant has
-- requested in writing that the insurer provide the report to the claimant and the insurer has failed to do so within a
-- reasonable time." Reasonable time is a judgment, asked.
@export Can I claim the fee for my treating doctor's first report on me (cl 28(3); Schedule 2 items 5 and 6)?
GIVEN `it is the first report by my treating doctor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the report is an initial report by a treating medical practitioner (your treating general practitioner or treating specialist)
      `I asked the insurer in writing to give me the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked the insurer in writing to provide that report to you
      `the insurer failed to give it to me within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer failed to provide the report to you within a reasonable time
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I claim the fee for my treating doctor's first report` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `it is the first report by my treating doctor`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside cl 28(3); the text is silent)
           IF `I asked the insurer in writing to give me the report` AND `the insurer failed to give it to me within a reasonable time` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- "may not ... unless"

§§ `cl 30, 31 -- costs after a claims assessment`

-- cl 30(1): applies if damages were assessed under Division 7.6 and "the claimant does not accept that amount ... within
-- 21 days after the certificate of assessment is issued". (2) If court awarded damages "do not exceed" the certificate,
-- the claimant pays the costs incurred by any party, "not exceeding $25,000 (or such other amount as is determined by the
-- Authority by order published in the Gazette)". (3) The insurer pays if court awarded damages exceed the certificate
-- "(a) ... by at least $2,000 or 20% (whichever is the greater), or (b) ... by at least $200,000." (4) "In any other case"
-- each pays its own. (5) Subject to any court direction. (8) Court awarded damages exclude interest and are after the
-- Act's Part 4 deductions. The 20% is read as 20% of the certificate amount (fork F15).
@export If I did not accept the assessed damages and went to court, who pays the costs incurred after the certificate (cl 30)?
GIVEN `I accepted the assessed damages within 21 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you accepted the amount of damages in the certificate of assessment, in settlement, within 21 days after the certificate was issued
      `the amount in the certificate of assessment` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of damages in the certificate of claims assessment, in dollars
      `the damages the court awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc All damages the court awarded you, without interest, after the deductions and reductions under Part 4 of the Act, in dollars
      `the court gave a direction as to costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court gave a direction as to who pays the costs
GIVETH A `Who pays the costs after court`
`Who pays the costs after I rejected the assessed damages` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I accepted the assessed damages within 21 days` THEN `clause 30 does not apply, because I accepted the assessed damages within 21 days`
           IF `the court gave a direction as to costs` THEN `the court's direction as to costs decides`
           IF `the damages the court awarded` AT MOST `the amount in the certificate of assessment` THEN `I must pay the costs any party incurred, up to the cap`
           IF     `the excess` AT LEAST (`the larger of` 2000 `and` (`the amount in the certificate of assessment` TIMES 20%))
               OR `the excess` AT LEAST 200000
           THEN `the insurer must pay the costs any party incurred`
           OTHERWISE `the insurer and I each pay our own costs`
    WHERE
        `the excess` MEANS `the damages the court awarded` MINUS `the amount in the certificate of assessment`

@export If I did not accept the assessed damages and went to court, what is the most I can be made to pay towards the costs the parties incurred after the certificate (cl 30(2))?
GIVEN `I accepted the assessed damages within 21 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you accepted the amount of damages in the certificate of assessment, in settlement, within 21 days after the certificate was issued
      `the amount in the certificate of assessment` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of damages in the certificate of claims assessment, in dollars
      `the damages the court awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc All damages the court awarded you, without interest, after the deductions and reductions under Part 4 of the Act, in dollars
      `the court gave a direction as to costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court gave a direction as to who pays the costs
      `the amount the Authority has set by Gazette order` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the State Insurance Regulatory Authority has set in place of $25,000 by order published in the Gazette, in dollars (0 if it has set none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most I can be made to pay in costs after rejecting the assessed damages` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Who pays the costs after I rejected the assessed damages` `I accepted the assessed damages within 21 days` `the amount in the certificate of assessment` `the damages the court awarded` `the court gave a direction as to costs`
    WHEN `I must pay the costs any party incurred, up to the cap` THEN
        IF `the amount the Authority has set by Gazette order` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN JUST `the amount the Authority has set by Gazette order`
        ELSE JUST 25000
    WHEN `the insurer must pay the costs any party incurred` THEN JUST 0
    WHEN `the insurer and I each pay our own costs` THEN JUST 0
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the court's direction decides, or cl 30 does not apply)

-- cl 31(1): applies if damages were assessed and "the insurer does not admit liability under the claim within 21 days
-- after the certificate of assessment is issued". (2) "Subject to any direction of a court as to costs, the insurer is
-- liable to pay the costs of the claimant incurred in respect of the claim and the maximum costs set out in this
-- Regulation do not apply in respect of those costs." (3) Not costs before the certificate.
@export If the insurer did not admit liability within 21 days after my claims assessment certificate, must it pay my costs from then on, without the maximum costs applying (cl 31)?
GIVEN `the insurer admitted liability within 21 days after the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer admitted liability under your claim within 21 days after the certificate of claims assessment was issued
      `the court gave a direction as to costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court gave a direction as to who pays the costs
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the insurer pay my costs because it did not admit liability` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the insurer admitted liability within 21 days after the certificate` THEN JUST FALSE  -- cl 31(1) unmet (fork F16)
           IF `the court gave a direction as to costs` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the court's direction decides)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `cl 34 -- treatment fees`

-- cl 34(1): the most an insurer is liable for a fee for treatment and care to which s 8.9 of the Act applies "is the
-- amount listed, in respect of the treatment concerned, in the AMA List". (2) Only for treatment and care provided by a
-- health practitioner and for which the AMA List specifies a fee. The note: s 8.9 does not apply to treatment at a
-- hospital paid to the hospital, but does apply to a private hospital's fee. The AMA List amount is asked.
@export What is the most the insurer must pay for this treatment fee (cl 34; Act s 8.9)?
GIVEN `a health practitioner provided the treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the treatment or care was provided to you by a health practitioner
      `it was at a public hospital and paid to the hospital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the treatment was provided at a hospital (other than a private hospital's own fee) and payment is made to the hospital rather than to the provider
      `the AMA List gives a fee for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the AMA List of Medical Services and Fees (as recognised by the Authority) specifies a fee for the treatment
      `the AMA List fee` IS A NUMBER @desc The fee the AMA List gives for the treatment, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most the insurer must pay for this treatment` MEANS
    IF `a health practitioner provided the treatment` AND (NOT `it was at a public hospital and paid to the hospital`) AND `the AMA List gives a fee for it`
    THEN JUST `the AMA List fee`
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside cl 34(2): the clause fixes no maximum)

§§ `cl 35 -- GST`

-- cl 35(1): a cost fixed by Part 6 "may be increased by the amount of any GST payable in respect of the service". (2) A
-- legal or medical practitioner may not charge or recover for GST "an amount that is greater than 10% of the maximum
-- amount payable under this Part".
@export With GST added, what is the most that can be charged for a service whose maximum the Regulation fixes (cl 35)?
GIVEN `the maximum without GST` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum cost or fee the Regulation fixes for the service, in dollars, before GST
      `the GST payable` IS A NUMBER @desc The GST payable on the service, in dollars
      `it is charged by a legal or medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charge is by an Australian legal practitioner or a medical practitioner
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most that can be charged with GST` MEANS
    IF `it is charged by a legal or medical practitioner`
    THEN `the maximum without GST` PLUS (`the smaller of` `the GST payable` `and` (`the maximum without GST` TIMES 10%))
    ELSE `the maximum without GST` PLUS `the GST payable`
